--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0402 has two parts:
- **Part B** (scorers) — `capacity_plausible_for_level` and `level_consistent_with_name`
  predicates, wired into `score_coherence()` and `sota_cross_eval.csv`. DONE (PR
  ticket/0402-model-emits-level).
- **Part A** (this ticket) — prompt change so each output row declares its
  granularity level (Unit/Block/Plant/Complex/Unknown), plus a one-call-per-regime
  audit before any batch, plus `measurements.jsonl` backfill for existing rows.

Until Part A lands, the Part-B scorers return `(None, "column_missing")` on all
existing data rows (no `level` column in current output). The feature is inert but
present; backfill activates it.

## Relevant files
- `src/aedist/reference_level.py` — `derive_reference_level()` for post-hoc name derivation
- `src/aedist/schema.py` — `Level` enum (0401)
- `experiments/experiments.toml` — sweep configs; prompt versions live here
- `experiments/derived/measurements.jsonl` — the file to backfill

## Actions

1. **Audit first** (`.claude/rules/workflow.md`): run ONE call per regime with the new
   prompt. Inspect whether models label grain coherently. If models cannot self-classify
   reliably, fall back to post-hoc name derivation via `derive_reference_level()` and
   record the fallback decision — do not ship a noisy hallucination axis.

2. **Prompt change**: add a `level` field (Unit/Block/Plant/Complex/Unknown) to the
   output row schema in the system prompt for each query variant. Document the exact
   prompt version bump.

3. **Backfill**: for existing `measurements.jsonl` rows lacking `level`, derive it
   post-hoc from the emitted name via `derive_reference_level()`. Flag backfilled rows
   as `level_source: "derived"` (vs. `"model"` for new runs). Wire into
   `records_to_metrics()` if required by ADR-7; at minimum document in the row's extra
   dict.

4. **Re-run sweep if audit passes**: only after confirming the grain audit verdict,
   gate whether a new Exp2 sweep with `level` is needed. If audit fails, ship derived
   fallback only and open a separate ticket for the sweep.

## Test
- After backfill: `load_metrics()` rows have `level` key populated for at least N
  existing rows.
- Adherence test: if `level` is added to `records_to_metrics()`, add it to the ADR-7
  wiring tests.

## Verification
- [ ] Prompt diff shows `level` field in the output schema instruction.
- [ ] Grain audit: at least one call per regime; output inspected and verdict recorded in ticket log.
- [ ] `measurements.jsonl` rows carry `level` (model or derived).
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Invariants
- Do not re-run the full sweep before the audit verdict is confirmed.
- Post-hoc derivation must be flagged as `level_source: "derived"`, not silently passed off as model-emitted.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Prompt emits `level`; one-call-per-regime audit recorded before any batch.
- [ ] `measurements.jsonl` rows carry `level` (model-emitted on new runs, derived +
      flagged on existing).
- [ ] `make check` passes.
